@*
    A column of lists to open: a few fixed at the top, then folds of them under
    group headings, then the rest. Every list carries how much is in it. It is
    the side navigation a To Do-style pane keeps on its left edge, and it owns
    nothing but the drawing — which row is selected, which groups are open and
    which row is being renamed are all the host's, asked for through a parameter
    and changed through a callback, so a host keeps whatever state model it
    already has. TreeView was not bent into this because a tree of chapters and a
    column of lists are two conventions, and one component telling both stories
    would tell neither well: this one has counts, a rename, a menu on every row
    and no folder to open.

    The rows are buttons, and Enter and Space are deliberately not handled in the
    keydown below: a button's own activation is the click handler, and a second
    copy of it on the key would select twice and — worse — fold a group open and
    closed again in one press. The keys this component does own are the ones a
    button has no answer for: the arrows walk the visible rows, Home and End jump
    to the ends, Right and Left open and close a group or step out of one, and F2
    asks the host to start a rename.

    Shift+F10 and the ContextMenu key are not in that list either, on purpose.
    A browser answers both with the same `contextmenu` event a right-click sends,
    dispatched at the focused row's own position, so one handler hears every way
    of asking for a menu and reports the same target with the same coordinates.
    A keydown copy would have opened the menu twice in every browser that does
    this, which is all of them.

    One tab stop. The selected row is the tabbable one, or the last row the
    keyboard visited, or the first row when neither applies — a column of ten
    lists that cost ten Tabs to cross would be ten stops between the reader and
    the content beside it.

    Groups fold with their own header rather than through FoldControl. The
    header is a row like any other — it takes the roving tabindex, the arrows,
    F2, and a right-click — and it turns into a rename field when asked, none of
    which a trigger owned by another component can be handed. What FoldControl
    would have given is drawn here on its own terms: aria-expanded on the
    header, aria-controls to the list it folds, and the list kept in the DOM and
    hidden rather than removed, so a fold does not throw away the rows a host may
    be measuring or anchoring into.

    A rename is a field in the row's place, not inside its button — an input
    inside a button is not markup any browser agrees on. Enter and blur commit,
    Escape cancels, and an unchanged or empty name is reported as a cancel rather
    than as a rename to the same thing, so a host never has to ask whether a
    commit meant anything. The field is focused with its text selected, which is
    what renaming means everywhere else in this library.
*@

@inject IJSRuntime Js

<nav class="@ClassValue"
     aria-label="@AriaLabel"
     data-testid="@TestId"
     @oncontextmenu="OnRootContextMenuAsync"
     @oncontextmenu:preventDefault="true"
     @attributes="AdditionalAttributes">

    @if (Fixed.Count > 0)
    {
        <ul class="@ListClassValue" data-testid="@Suffix("fixed")">
            @foreach (var entry in Fixed)
            {
                @RenderEntry(entry, null)
            }
        </ul>
    }

    @for (var i = 0; i < Groups.Count; i++)
    {
        @RenderGroup(Groups[i], i)
    }

    @if (Ungrouped.Count > 0)
    {
        <ul class="@ListClassValue" data-testid="@Suffix("ungrouped")">
            @foreach (var entry in Ungrouped)
            {
                @RenderEntry(entry, null)
            }
        </ul>
    }
</nav>

@code {
    private readonly string _id = "list-nav-" + Guid.NewGuid().ToString("N");

    /// <summary>The element behind every row, by id, for the focus moves. Pruned
    /// to the rows the parameters still name on every parameter set, because a
    /// row a host deletes never renders again and its reference would otherwise
    /// stay here for the life of the component.</summary>
    private readonly Dictionary<string, ElementReference> _rows = [];

    /// <summary>How many row references are being held, for the test that pins
    /// the pruning; nothing else reads it.</summary>
    internal int TrackedRowCount => _rows.Count;

    /// <summary>The row the keyboard last stood on, which is the row Tab comes
    /// back to. Set by focus rather than by the arrows alone so a row reached
    /// with the mouse counts too.</summary>
    private string? _activeId;

    /// <summary>A row to focus once the render that made it tabbable has been
    /// applied. Asked for in the key handler, done after the render, for the
    /// reason GraphAtlasIndex gives: the element the focus is meant for is only
    /// certainly there once the batch is.</summary>
    private string? _focusRequestId;

    /// <summary>Which row the open field belongs to, remembered so a change of
    /// <see cref="EditingId"/> can be told apart from a re-render with the same
    /// one — the draft is seeded once per rename, not once per render.</summary>
    private string? _editingFor;

    private string _draft = string.Empty;

    /// <summary>The field has just been rendered and has not been focused yet.
    /// Once per opening: a re-render mid-typing must not drag the caret back over
    /// the name.</summary>
    private bool _focusRename;

    /// <summary>Enter or Escape has already settled the open rename, so the blur
    /// the browser may send as the field is taken away says nothing new. Without
    /// it a rename committed on Enter could be committed again as the host closed
    /// the field, and a rename abandoned on Escape could be committed on its way
    /// out.</summary>
    private bool _settled;

    /// <summary>The rows above every group: the lists a host always shows, in
    /// the order given.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<ListNavEntry> Fixed { get; set; } = [];

    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<ListNavGroup> Groups { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The rows under every group: lists filed under no heading.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public IReadOnlyList<ListNavEntry> Ungrouped { get; set; } = [];

    /// <summary>The entry the pane is showing. Selection is the host's state,
    /// which is why this is a value and <see cref="OnSelect"/> is how it
    /// changes; the component marks the row and never decides which.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? SelectedId { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Whether a group is open, asked per group. Closed for every group
    /// until a host says otherwise.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public Func<string, bool> IsGroupExpanded { get; set; } = static _ => false;

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnSelect { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnToggleGroup { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A menu was asked for: on a row, on a group heading, or on the
    /// empty area under the rows — the root, where "new list" lives. The
    /// coordinates are the pointer's, or the row's own when the keyboard asked,
    /// ready to hand to a ContextMenu as they are.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<(ListNavTarget Target, double X, double Y)> OnContextMenu { get; set; }

    /// <summary>F2 on a row. The component does not open the field itself:
    /// whether a row may be renamed at all is the host's rule, and it answers by
    /// setting <see cref="EditingId"/>.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<string> OnRenameRequested { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The entry or group whose name is a field right now, or null. A
    /// value naming no row renders no field.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? EditingId { get; set; }

    /// <summary>A rename settled on a new, non-empty name. The name is trimmed.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback<(string Id, string Name)> OnRenameCommitted { get; set; }

    /// <summary>The rename ended with nothing to apply: Escape, or a commit whose
    /// name was empty or the one the row already had. The host closes the field
    /// on either, which is why the two are one callback.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public EventCallback OnRenameCancelled { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? AriaLabel { get; set; }

    [Parameter]
    public string? CssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Replaces <c>list-nav</c> on the nav, and the stem every inner
    /// class is built on.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string BaseClass { get; set; } = "list-nav";

    /// <summary>Lands on the nav. Every row gets <c>{TestId}-{id}</c>, every
    /// count <c>{TestId}-{id}-count</c>, the open rename field
    /// <c>{TestId}-rename</c>, and the two loose lists <c>{TestId}-fixed</c> and
    /// <c>{TestId}-ungrouped</c>.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? TestId { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Replaces <c>list-nav__list</c> on every list of rows.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? ListCssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Replaces <c>list-nav__item</c> on the element holding a row.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? ItemCssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Replaces <c>list-nav__row</c> on an entry's button.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? RowCssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Replaces <c>list-nav__row list-nav__row--selected</c> on the
    /// selected entry's button.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? SelectedRowCssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Replaces <c>list-nav__group</c> on the element holding a group's
    /// header and its list.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? GroupCssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Replaces <c>list-nav__row list-nav__row--group</c> on a group's
    /// header button.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? GroupHeaderCssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Replaces <c>list-nav__icon</c> on an entry's glyph.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? IconCssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Replaces <c>list-nav__label</c> on every row's text.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? LabelCssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Replaces <c>list-nav__count</c> on every count. The count is a
    /// Badge with this as its base class, so a host's own badge naming lands on
    /// exactly the element it expects.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? CountCssClass { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Replaces <c>list-nav__rename</c> on the open rename field's input.</summary>
    [Parameter]
    public string? RenameCssClass { get; set; }

    [Parameter(CaptureUnmatchedValues = true)]
    public IReadOnlyDictionary<string, object>? AdditionalAttributes { get; set; }

    private string Base => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(BaseClass) ? "list-nav" : BaseClass;

    private string ClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CssClass) ? Base : $"{Base} {CssClass}";

    private string ListClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(ListCssClass) ? Base + "__list" : ListCssClass;

    private string ItemClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(ItemCssClass) ? Base + "__item" : ItemCssClass;

    private string RowClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(RowCssClass) ? Base + "__row" : RowCssClass;

    private string SelectedRowClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(SelectedRowCssClass)
        ? $"{Base}__row {Base}__row--selected"
        : SelectedRowCssClass;

    private string GroupClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(GroupCssClass) ? Base + "__group" : GroupCssClass;

    private string GroupHeaderClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(GroupHeaderCssClass)
        ? $"{Base}__row {Base}__row--group"
        : GroupHeaderCssClass;

    private string IconClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(IconCssClass) ? Base + "__icon" : IconCssClass;

    private string LabelClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(LabelCssClass) ? Base + "__label" : LabelCssClass;

    private string CountClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(CountCssClass) ? Base + "__count" : CountCssClass;

    private string RenameClassValue => string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(RenameCssClass) ? Base + "__rename" : RenameCssClass;

    private string EditingRowClassValue => $"{RowClassValue} {Base}__row--editing";

    private string ChevronClass(bool expanded) =>
        expanded ? $"{Base}__chevron {Base}__chevron--open" : Base + "__chevron";

    private string RenameFieldId => _id + "-rename";

    private string HeaderId(int index) => $"{_id}-group-{index}";

    private string RegionId(int index) => $"{_id}-region-{index}";

    private string? Suffix(string part) => TestId is null ? null : $"{TestId}-{part}";

    private bool IsSelected(ListNavEntry entry) =>
        SelectedId is not null && string.Equals(entry.Id, SelectedId, StringComparison.Ordinal);

    private bool IsEditing(string id) =>
        EditingId is not null && string.Equals(id, EditingId, StringComparison.Ordinal);

    /// <summary>One row of the walk the arrows take: what it is and, for an
    /// entry under a heading, which heading — so Left knows where to step out to.</summary>
    private readonly record struct Row(string Id, bool IsGroup, string? GroupId);

    /// <summary>The rows in reading order, minus the ones a closed group hides.
    /// Recomputed per key press rather than cached: it is a handful of records,
    /// and a cache would be one more thing to invalidate when a host folds a
    /// group between two presses.</summary>
    private List<Row> VisibleRows
    {
        get
        {
            var rows = new List<Row>();

            foreach (var entry in Fixed) rows.Add(new Row(entry.Id, false, null));

            foreach (var group in Groups)
            {
                rows.Add(new Row(group.Id, true, null));

                if (!IsGroupExpanded(group.Id)) continue;

                foreach (var entry in group.Entries) rows.Add(new Row(entry.Id, false, group.Id));
            }

            foreach (var entry in Ungrouped) rows.Add(new Row(entry.Id, false, null));

            return rows;
        }
    }

    /// <summary>The one row Tab lands on. The keyboard's last row while it is
    /// still on screen, else the selected row, else the first — each a fallback
    /// for the one above it going out of view when a group folds.</summary>
    private string? TabbableId
    {
        get
        {
            var rows = VisibleRows;
            if (rows.Count == 0) return null;

            if (_activeId is { } active && rows.Any(row => row.Id == active)) return active;
            if (SelectedId is { } selected && rows.Any(row => row.Id == selected)) return selected;

            return rows[0].Id;
        }
    }

    private int TabIndexOf(string id) => string.Equals(id, TabbableId, StringComparison.Ordinal) ? 0 : -1;

    private string? LabelOf(string id)
    {
        foreach (var entry in Fixed) if (entry.Id == id) return entry.Label;

        foreach (var group in Groups)
        {
            if (group.Id == id) return group.Label;
            foreach (var entry in group.Entries) if (entry.Id == id) return entry.Label;
        }

        foreach (var entry in Ungrouped) if (entry.Id == id) return entry.Label;

        return null;
    }

    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        PruneRows();

        if (string.Equals(EditingId, _editingFor, StringComparison.Ordinal)) return;

        // The field that was open is closing, or another is opening in its
        // place. Either way the row the closed one stood in gets the focus back
        // — it is the trigger a rename was dismissed from, and a dismissal that
        // left the focus on nothing would strand a keyboard reader at the top of
        // the page. Nothing to do when that row is gone: a rename can end with a
        // delete, and a reference to a removed element is not worth chasing.
        if (_editingFor is { } closing && EditingId is null)
        {
            _activeId = closing;
            _focusRequestId = closing;
        }

        _editingFor = EditingId;
        _settled = false;
        _draft = EditingId is null ? string.Empty : LabelOf(EditingId) ?? string.Empty;
        _focusRename = EditingId is not null;
    }

    /// <summary>Drops the reference of every row the parameters no longer
    /// name. The rows that remain are re-captured by the render that follows,
    /// so nothing the focus needs is lost.</summary>
    private void PruneRows()
    {
        if (_rows.Count == 0) return;

        var current = new HashSet<string>(StringComparer.Ordinal);

        foreach (var entry in Fixed) current.Add(entry.Id);

        foreach (var group in Groups)
        {
            current.Add(group.Id);
            foreach (var entry in group.Entries) current.Add(entry.Id);
        }

        foreach (var entry in Ungrouped) current.Add(entry.Id);

        foreach (var id in _rows.Keys.Where(id => !current.Contains(id)).ToList())
        {
            _rows.Remove(id);
        }
    }

    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (_focusRename)
        {
            _focusRename = false;
            await QuickEditField.FocusAsync(Js, RenameFieldId);
        }

        if (_focusRequestId is not { } id) return;

        _focusRequestId = null;

        if (!_rows.TryGetValue(id, out var row)) return;

        try
        {
            await row.FocusAsync();
        }
        catch (JSException)
        {
            // The row this reference pointed at is no longer in the document.
        }
        catch (JSDisconnectedException)
        {
            // The circuit went away between the key press and the render.
        }
        catch (InvalidOperationException)
        {
            // Prerendering: there is no element to focus yet.
        }
    }

    private Task OnRootContextMenuAsync(MouseEventArgs e) =>
        OnContextMenu.InvokeAsync((ListNavTarget.Root, e.ClientX, e.ClientY));

    private Task OnRowContextMenuAsync(MouseEventArgs e, ListNavTarget target) =>
        OnContextMenu.InvokeAsync((target, e.ClientX, e.ClientY));

    private void RequestFocus(List<Row> rows, int index)
    {
        if (rows.Count == 0) return;

        var target = rows[Math.Clamp(index, 0, rows.Count - 1)].Id;
        _activeId = target;
        _focusRequestId = target;
    }

    private async Task OnRowKeyDownAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e, Row row)
    {
        var rows = VisibleRows;
        var index = rows.FindIndex(candidate => candidate.Id == row.Id);
        if (index < 0) return;

        switch (e.Key)
        {
            case "ArrowDown":
                RequestFocus(rows, index + 1);
                break;

            case "ArrowUp":
                RequestFocus(rows, index - 1);
                break;

            case "Home":
                RequestFocus(rows, 0);
                break;

            case "End":
                RequestFocus(rows, rows.Count - 1);
                break;

            case "ArrowRight":
                // On a heading, Right opens; on an open heading it steps onto the
                // first row inside, if there is one — the tree convention, and
                // the one a reader who has met TreeView already expects.
                if (!row.IsGroup) break;

                if (!IsGroupExpanded(row.Id))
                {
                    await OnToggleGroup.InvokeAsync(row.Id);
                }
                else if (index + 1 < rows.Count && rows[index + 1].GroupId == row.Id)
                {
                    RequestFocus(rows, index + 1);
                }

                break;

            case "ArrowLeft":
                // Left closes an open heading, and from a row inside a group
                // steps back out to its heading. On any other row it is nothing.
                if (row.IsGroup)
                {
                    if (IsGroupExpanded(row.Id)) await OnToggleGroup.InvokeAsync(row.Id);
                }
                else if (row.GroupId is { } groupId)
                {
                    RequestFocus(rows, rows.FindIndex(candidate => candidate.Id == groupId));
                }

                break;

            case "F2":
                await OnRenameRequested.InvokeAsync(row.Id);
                break;
        }
    }

    private Task OnRenameKeyDownAsync(KeyboardEventArgs e) => e.Key switch
    {
        "Enter" => CommitRenameAsync(),
        "Escape" => CancelRenameAsync(),
        _ => Task.CompletedTask
    };

    /// <summary>The blur's commit, which is the only one the settled flag
    /// guards. Enter is not guarded by it: a host that refuses a name and keeps
    /// the field open has to be able to hear the next Enter.</summary>
    private Task OnRenameBlurAsync() => _settled ? Task.CompletedTask : CommitRenameAsync();

    private async Task CommitRenameAsync()
    {
        if (_editingFor is not { } id) return;

        _settled = true;

        var name = _draft.Trim();

        if (name.Length == 0 || string.Equals(name, LabelOf(id), StringComparison.Ordinal))
        {
            await OnRenameCancelled.InvokeAsync();
            return;
        }

        await OnRenameCommitted.InvokeAsync((id, name));
    }

    private async Task CancelRenameAsync()
    {
        if (_editingFor is null) return;

        _settled = true;
        await OnRenameCancelled.InvokeAsync();
    }

    private RenderFragment RenderEntry(ListNavEntry entry, string? groupId) => @<li class="@ItemClassValue">
        @if (IsEditing(entry.Id))
        {
            @RenderRename(entry.Id, entry.Icon, entry.Count)
        }
        else
        {
            var selected = IsSelected(entry);
            var row = new Row(entry.Id, false, groupId);

            <button type="button"
                    class="@(selected ? SelectedRowClassValue : RowClassValue)"
                    data-testid="@Suffix(entry.Id)"
                    aria-current="@(selected ? "true" : null)"
                    tabindex="@TabIndexOf(entry.Id)"
                    @ref="_rows[entry.Id]"
                    @onclick="() => OnSelect.InvokeAsync(entry.Id)"
                    @onfocus="() => _activeId = entry.Id"
                    @onkeydown="e => OnRowKeyDownAsync(e, row)"
                    @oncontextmenu="e => OnRowContextMenuAsync(e, ListNavTarget.Entry(entry.Id))"
                    @oncontextmenu:preventDefault="true"
                    @oncontextmenu:stopPropagation="true">
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(entry.Icon))
                {
                    <span class="@IconClassValue" aria-hidden="true">@entry.Icon</span>
                }
                <span class="@LabelClassValue">@entry.Label</span>
                @RenderCount(entry.Id, entry.Count)
            </button>
        }
    </li>;

    private RenderFragment RenderGroup(ListNavGroup group, int index) => @<div class="@GroupClassValue" data-testid="@Suffix(group.Id + "-group")">
        @{
            var expanded = IsGroupExpanded(group.Id);
            var row = new Row(group.Id, true, null);
        }
        @if (IsEditing(group.Id))
        {
            @RenderRename(group.Id, null, null)
        }
        else
        {
            <button type="button"
                    class="@GroupHeaderClassValue"
                    id="@HeaderId(index)"
                    data-testid="@Suffix(group.Id)"
                    aria-expanded="@(expanded ? "true" : "false")"
                    aria-controls="@RegionId(index)"
                    tabindex="@TabIndexOf(group.Id)"
                    @ref="_rows[group.Id]"
                    @onclick="() => OnToggleGroup.InvokeAsync(group.Id)"
                    @onfocus="() => _activeId = group.Id"
                    @onkeydown="e => OnRowKeyDownAsync(e, row)"
                    @oncontextmenu="e => OnRowContextMenuAsync(e, ListNavTarget.Group(group.Id))"
                    @oncontextmenu:preventDefault="true"
                    @oncontextmenu:stopPropagation="true">
                <span class="@ChevronClass(expanded)" aria-hidden="true">&#9656;</span>
                <span class="@LabelClassValue">@group.Label</span>
            </button>
        }
        @* Kept in the DOM and hidden, rather than removed, so a host that
           measures or anchors into the list does not lose it on every fold. *@
        <ul class="@ListClassValue" id="@RegionId(index)" aria-labelledby="@HeaderId(index)" hidden="@(!expanded)">
            @foreach (var entry in group.Entries)
            {
                @RenderEntry(entry, group.Id)
            }
        </ul>
    </div>;

    /// <summary>The count, as a Badge wearing this component's own class. A
    /// count that stays on a row being renamed is deliberate: the number is a
    /// fact about the list, not about its name.</summary>
    private RenderFragment RenderCount(string id, int count) =>
        @<Badge BaseClass="@CountClassValue"
                Kind=""
                CssClass="@(count == 0 ? CountClassValue + "--zero" : null)"
                TestId="@Suffix(id + "-count")">@count</Badge>;

    /// <summary>The row with a field where its name was. The right-click is
    /// stopped here and not prevented: a menu asked for inside a field is the
    /// browser's cut-and-paste menu, which is the one the reader wants there.</summary>
    private RenderFragment RenderRename(string id, string? icon, int? count) => @<div class="@EditingRowClassValue"
             data-testid="@Suffix(id + "-editing")"
             @oncontextmenu:stopPropagation="true">
        @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(icon))
        {
            <span class="@IconClassValue" aria-hidden="true">@icon</span>
        }
        <TextField Value="@_draft"
                   ValueChanged="value => _draft = value"
                   AriaLabel="@($"Rename {LabelOf(id)}")"
                   Bare="true"
                   Compact="true"
                   InputCssClass="@RenameClassValue"
                   Id="@RenameFieldId"
                   TestId="@Suffix("rename")"
                   @onkeydown="OnRenameKeyDownAsync"
                   @onblur="OnRenameBlurAsync" />
        @if (count is { } value)
        {
            @RenderCount(id, value)
        }
    </div>;
}
